    "result_text": "The change is complete and the build is green. There's only one test class in the project (`AcceptanceTest`), and it passes.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required all rejection responses (400, 409, 429) to return an RFC7807 `application/problem+json` body with `type`, `title`, `status`, and `detail`.\n\n**Root cause:** In `ExceptionControllerAdvice`, the `handleRejectedRequestException` handler \u2014 which owns the business-rule rejections that produce 400/409/429 (thrown as `RejectedRequestException` from `OwnerRestControllerV1.createNewOwner`) \u2014 returned `ResponseEntity<Void>` with a bare status and **no body**. The other client-error handlers (`MethodArgumentNotValidException` \u2192 400, `DataIntegrityViolationException`) already returned a `ProblemDetail`.\n\n**Fix** (`ExceptionControllerAdvice.java`):\n- Changed the handler's return type from `ResponseEntity<Void>` to `ResponseEntity<ProblemDetail>`.\n- Built the body via the existing `detailBuild(...)` helper, which populates all four required members (`type`, `title`, `status`, `detail`), passing the rejection's own `HttpStatus` so the status is preserved unchanged.\n- Added an `ERROR_REQUEST_REJECTED` detail constant for the message.\n\nReturning a `ProblemDetail` makes Spring emit the `application/problem+json` content type automatically, matching the acceptance test's assertions (content type + `$.status`). HTTP status codes are unchanged.",
